    ('DOLCETTO', 'Sweet Little One', 'Early-ripening Italian black grape yielding fruity, round, and dry red wines.', "Name translates to 'little sweet one' in Italian, referring to the sweet ripe grape berries."),
    ('DRAGONFRUIT', 'Pitahaya', 'Vibrant magenta cactus fruit with green scales and white or red speckled flesh.', 'Mild, refreshing kiwi-like flavor; harvested from night-blooming Hylocereus cacti.'),
    ('DRUPELET', 'Tiny Drupe', 'One of the small individual stone fruit segments that make up an aggregate berry.', 'Each tiny round bubble on a blackberry or raspberry contains its own miniature seed.'),
    ('DUKU', 'Lansium Fruit', 'Sweet, translucent segmented fruit native to Southeast Asia with thin skin.', 'Closely related to langsat; eaten fresh by popping segments from the peel.'),
    ('DUNCAN', 'Heritage Grapefruit', 'The oldest recognized grapefruit cultivar, famous for intense flavor and seeds.', 'Named after AL Duncan; heralded by fruit connoisseurs for exceptional sweetness.'),
    ('DURIAN', 'King with Odor', 'Spiky tropical fruit famous for intense, pungent sulfurous odor and rich custard flesh.', 'Banned on public transit in Southeast Asia, yet revered by locals as the king of fruits.'),
    ('EGREMONT', 'English Russet Apple', 'Small, round English dessert apple with textured golden-russet skin and nutty bite.', 'Known as the Egremont Russet; pairs classically with sharp cheddar cheese.'),
    ('ELBERTA', 'Classic Yellow Peach', 'Famous American heirloom peach variety with yellow flesh and red blush.', 'Introduced in Georgia in 1870; the historic gold standard for canning peaches.'),
    ('ELDERBERRY', 'Dark Cluster Berry', 'Tiny, dark purple berry growing in heavy hanging umbel clusters on elder bushes.', 'Simmered into soothing immune-supporting syrups to treat winter colds and flus.'),
    ('ELEPHANTAPPLE', 'Dillenia Fruit', 'Hard, large green tropical fruit with thick overlapping fleshy sepals.', 'Used in Assamese curries and fish stews for its pleasant green apple sourness.'),
    ('EMPIRE', 'New York Apple', 'Cross between McIntosh and Red Delicious bred at Cornell University in 1945.', 'Possesses a dark red blush over green and sweet, juicy, crisp white flesh.'),
    ('ENDOCARP', 'Inner Pit', 'The innermost layer of the pericarp of a fruit that directly surrounds seeds.', 'Forms the hard, woody stone pit of a peach or the papery seed chamber of an apple.'),
    ('ENTOWEK', 'Red Wild Jackfruit', 'Wild tropical fruit from Borneo featuring vibrant red, fleshy sweet arils.', 'Grows deep in virgin rainforests, highly sought after by local indigenous foragers.'),
    ('EUREKA', 'Commercial Lemon', 'The most widely cultivated commercial supermarket lemon in the Western world.', 'Bears fruit year-round with bright yellow skin, acidic juice, and few seeds.'),
    ('EXOCARP', 'Outer Skin', 'The outermost botanical layer of the pericarp of a fruit, forming the skin.', 'Protects developing fruits from fungal infections, insects, and solar sunburn.'),
    ('FAIRCHILD', 'Early Mandarin Cross', 'Richly flavored hybrid cross between Clementine mandarin and Orlando tangelo.', 'Deep orange pebbled peel enclosing sweet, highly aromatic, richly pigmented pulp.'),
    ('FALLGLO', 'Autumn Tangerine', 'Early-ripening tangerine hybrid cross of Bower mandarin and Temple tangelo.', 'Harvested in October in Florida; deep orange skin with juicy tart-sweet flavor.'),
    ('FANTASIA', 'Freestone Nectarine', 'Classic California yellow nectarine with brilliant red blush and melting flesh.', 'Ripens in mid-summer; sweet and tangy with heavy juice yields.'),
    ('FEIJOA', 'Pineapple Guava', 'Small green oval fruit native to South America with an intoxicating perfume aroma.', 'Scooped with a spoon to eat the sweet, aromatic jelly center smelling of guava and mint.'),
    ('FIANO', 'Ancient Italian Grape', 'Ancient white grape cultivated in Campania, Italy, since ancient Roman times.', 'Honeybees love the sweet grapes, giving rise to its Latin name Vitis apiana.'),
    ('FIG', 'Inverted Flower', 'Soft, sweet pear-shaped fruit with chewy skin and crunchy seeds inside.', 'Botanically an inverted inflorescence (syconium) pollinated by specialized tiny fig wasps.'),
    ('FINGERLIME', 'Citrus Caviar', 'Slender Australian rainforest fruit containing caviar-like translucent juice vesicles.', 'When cut open, tiny round juice pearls pop with vibrant lime acidity on the palate.'),
    ('FLAVORTOP', 'Gourmet Nectarine', 'Large, sweet yellow freestone nectarine with bright crimson skin and rich flavor.', 'Consistently wins fruit tastings for its luscious balance of sugars and peach acids.'),
    ('FLESH', 'Edible Pulp', 'The soft, succulent, edible substance of a fruit between skin and seed.', 'Packed with water, natural sugars, vitamins, and refreshing fruit acids.'),
    ('FORELLE', 'Trout Pear', 'Small, sweet heirloom pear characterized by red freckles resembling a rainbow trout.', 'One of the oldest European pear varieties, turning golden yellow with scarlet speckles.'),
    ('FOXBERRY', 'Mountain Cranberry', 'Low-growing wild red berry fruit harvested across northern boreal forests.', 'Another name for lingonberry; makes delicious preserves for roast game meats.'),
    ('FRUCTOSE', 'Fruit Sugar', 'Simple ketonic monosaccharide sugar found naturally in honey, tree fruits, and berries.', 'The sweetest of all naturally occurring carbohydrate sugars on Earth.'),
    ('FRUIT', 'Botanical Structure', 'The seed-bearing structure in flowering plants formed from the ovary after flowering.', 'Provides sweet nourishment to animals that disperse the seeds within.'),
    ('FUERTE', 'Winter Avocado', 'Historic California avocado cultivar with smooth green skin and rich creamy texture.', 'The leading commercial avocado before being surpassed by the bumpy Hass variety.'),
    ('FUJI', 'Japanese Apple', 'Crisp, sweet apple variety developed in Japan by crossbreeding Red Delicious and Ralls.', 'Known for exceptional shelf life and refreshing, honey-sweet crunch.'),
    ('GALA', 'Sweet Apple', 'Mildly sweet apple with red-orange striped skin developed in New Zealand in the 1930s.', 'A favorite lunchbox snacking apple with thin skin and aromatic crispness.'),
    ('GALIA', 'Hybrid Sweet Melon', 'Green-fleshed hybrid melon with netted golden rind developed in Israel in 1973.', 'Combines the sweet green flesh of honeydew with the netting aroma of cantaloupe.'),
    ('GAMAY', 'Beaujolais Grape', 'Purple grape variety producing light-bodied, fruity red wines in Beaujolais.', 'Celebrated worldwide every November during festive Beaujolais Nouveau celebrations.'),
    ('GANDARIA', 'Plum Mango', 'Small Indonesian fruit looking like a miniature mango with an edible skin.', 'The entire fruit including purple interior seed is eaten fresh or pickled.'),
    ('GARCINIA', 'Mangosteen Genus', 'Genus of tropical evergreen trees producing sweet-sour fruits and gamboge resin.', 'Includes mangosteen, kokum, and achachairu, rich in natural xanthone antioxidants.'),
    ('GENIP', 'Spanish Lime', 'Small green fruit with a brittle shell enclosing sweet, tangy orange pulp.', 'Popular Caribbean street snack, sucked from the shell around a large seed.'),
    ('GLENN', 'Peach Mango', 'Florida mango cultivar celebrated for its sweet, silky flesh with hints of peach.', 'Mild, sweet, and highly aromatic tree prized by tropical home gardeners.'),
    ('GOJIBERRY', 'Wolfberry', 'Bright orange-red ellipsoidal berry cultivated in Ningxia, China, hailed as a superfood.', 'Dried like raisins; treasured in Chinese medicine to nourish eyes and longevity.'),
    ('GOLDENDELICIOUS', 'Sweet Yellow Apple', 'Pale green to golden-yellow apple discovered in West Virginia in 1905.', 'Naturally sweet, versatile apple suitable for fresh salads, baking, and cider.'),
    ('GOOSEBERRY', 'Translucent Berry', 'Ribbed, translucent green or purple berry with a tart, refreshing flavor.', 'Often baked into traditional summer crumbles, tarts, and fool desserts with cream.'),
    ('GOUBERRY', 'Silverberry Relative', 'Small red berry speckled with silver dots growing on Elaeagnus bushes.', 'Juicy, sweet-tart flavor with high lycopene content; eaten fresh or in jams.'),
    ('GOURD', 'Hard-Shelled Fruit', 'Hard-shelled fleshy fruit belonging to the Cucurbitaceae plant family.', 'Dried into durable musical instruments, ladles, containers, and birdhouses.'),
    ('GRANNY', 'Green Tart Apple', 'Crisp, bright green apple variety with a famously sharp, acidic punch.', 'Discovered in Australia by Maria Ann Smith in 1868; the classic pie apple.'),
    ('GRAPE', 'Vine Berry', 'Small smooth-skinned sweet berry growing in hanging bunches on woody vines.', 'Eaten fresh as table grapes, dried into raisins, or fermented into fine wines.'),
    ('GRAPEFRUIT', 'Tart-Sweet Citrus', 'Large, round citrus fruit known for slightly bitter, tart, and acidic pink flesh.', 'So named because fruits grow in hanging clusters resembling giant bunches of grapes.'),
    ('GRAVENSTEIN', 'Danish Heritage Apple', 'Celebrated heirloom apple with green-yellow skin washed in red stripes.', 'Unsurpassed for homemade applesauce, fresh cider, and traditional pies.'),
    ('GREENGAGE', 'Sweet Green Plum', 'Small, rounded plum variety with pale green or yellowish skin and rich syrup flesh.', 'Regarded by French culinary chefs as one of the sweetest, finest dessert plums.'),
    ('GRENACHE', 'Sun-Loving Grape', 'Late-ripening red grape variety thriving in hot Mediterranean climates like Rhone.', 'Contributes sweet raspberry and white pepper notes to Chateauneuf-du-Pape blends.'),
    ('GROVE', 'Citrus Field', 'Small wood, orchard, or group of trees, especially fruit or nut trees.', 'Famous Florida and California orange and lemon groves perfume spring breezes.'),
    ('GUABA', 'Ice Cream Bean Pod', 'Long ridged green tree pod enclosing soft, sweet white cottony pulp around seeds.', 'A beloved refreshing sweet treat sold on street corners in Andean South America.'),
    ('GUAMO', 'Ice Cream Pod', 'Leguminous tree pod containing sweet, fluffy white pulp around black seeds.', 'Beloved across tropical South America for its sweet, sugary dessert-like aril.'),
    ('GUAVA', 'Fragrant Tropical Fruit', 'Round tropical fruit with sweet, aromatic pink or white flesh and tiny hard seeds.', 'Possesses a strong, sweet floral aroma; eaten fresh or cooked into guava paste paste.'),
    ('GWEN', 'Compact Avocado Tree', 'Dwarf avocado variety producing fruit similar in taste and texture to Hass.', 'Ideal for small home gardens and containers, yielding rich nutty green fruit.'),
    ('HABANERO', 'Lantern Pepper', 'Small, fiery orange chili pepper with a distinctive fruity, floral heat.', 'Ranges from 100,000 to 350,000 Scoville Heat Units; popular in Caribbean hot sauces.'),
    ('HADEN', 'Parent of Florida Mangoes', 'Historic Florida mango cultivar that gave rise to dozens of modern varieties.', 'Seedling planted in Coconut Grove in 1902 that transformed commercial mango farming.'),
    ('HARALSON', 'Cold Hardy Apple', 'Tart, crisp winter apple bred by the University of Minnesota for harsh winters.', 'Firm, juicy, and acid; stores exceptionally well into spring root cellars.'),
    ('HARDIRED', 'Cold-Hardy Nectarine', 'Cold-hardy nectarine cultivar bred to withstand chilly northern winter freezes.', 'Produces sweet, juicy yellow-fleshed fruit with deep red skin in home gardens.'),
    ('HASS', 'Pebbled Avocado', 'The most popular commercial avocado cultivar, featuring dark pebbly skin when ripe.', 'Discovered by California postman Rudolph Hass; prized for creamy, high-oil flesh.'),
    ('HAWTHORN', 'Thorny Berry', 'Small red berry fruit growing on thorny hedgerow bushes across the countryside.', 'Known as haws; used in Chinese candied skewers called tanghulu and heart tonics.'),
    ('HAZELNUT', 'Filbert Nut', 'Rich, sweet spherical nut encased in a hard shell with a fringed outer husk.', 'Pairs famously with cocoa to produce decadent chocolate-hazelnut spreads.'),
    ('HIMSAGAR', 'Bengal Mango', 'Beloved mango cultivar from West Bengal and Bangladesh with silky fiberless pulp.', 'A short-season culinary gem with rich golden interior and deep sweet flavor.'),
    ('HONEYCRISP', 'Juicy Apple', 'Celebrated apple cultivar bred at University of Minnesota for explosive crispness.', 'Features exceptionally large cells that rupture when bitten, releasing a burst of juice.'),
    ('HONEYDEW', 'Smooth Green Melon', 'Round melon with a smooth, pale cream-green rind and sweet, pale green flesh.', 'Sweet and aromatic; popular in fresh fruit salads and chilled breakfast melon bowls.'),
    ('HOSUI', 'Juicy Russet Pear', 'Large Japanese Asian pear with a golden-bronze skin and sweet-tart juice.', 'Ripens in late summer, offering a refreshing burst of sweet juice when bitten.'),
    ('HUCKLEBERRY', 'Wild Mountain Berry', 'Small wild blue or purple berry native to mountain slopes of western North America.', 'Grizzly bears feast on mountain huckleberries; cannot be easily cultivated commercially.'),
    ('HUDSON', 'Late Winter Cherry', 'Very late-maturing sweet dark cherry variety discovered in Hudson Valley, New York.', 'Extends the fresh cherry season into late summer with firm, sweet black fruit.'),
    ('IDARED', 'Idaho Red Apple', 'Bright red winter apple bred in Moscow, Idaho, by crossing Jonathan and Wagener.', 'Possesses crisp, fine-grained tart flesh that retains its shape in cooking.'),
    ('ILAMA', 'Central American Fruit', 'Tropical fruit native to Central America with either pink or white sweet pulp.', 'Eaten chilled by scooping out the custard-like sweet flesh with a spoon.'),
    ('INGA', 'Ice Cream Bean', 'Long green tree pod containing fluffy white pulp tasting like vanilla ice cream.', 'Native to the Amazon basin; seeds and sweet cottony arils are eaten fresh.'),
    ('IVYGOURD', 'Tindora', 'Small, smooth green vine fruit resembling a miniature cucumber in tropical Asia.', 'Crisp and juicy; sliced into spicy stir-fries or eaten raw with dipping salts.'),
    ('JABUTICABA', 'Brazilian Grape Tree', 'Purple-black grape-like fruit that grows directly on the trunk and bark of trees.', 'Cauliflorous tree produces fruit directly from its wood, eaten fresh or fermented.'),
    ('JACKFRUIT', 'Colossal Tree Fruit', 'The largest tree-borne fruit in the world, capable of weighing up to 80 pounds.', 'Young unripe jackfruit has a meaty texture widely used as a plant-based pork substitute.'),
    ('JAFFA', 'Middle Eastern Orange', 'Famous sweet orange variety with a thick peel developed by Arab farmers near Jaffa.', 'Highly exported across the Mediterranean for centuries for its sweet, seedless juice.'),
    ('JALAPENO', 'Classic Green Chili', 'Medium-sized green chili pepper famous for moderate heat and crisp texture.', 'Smoked and dried jalapenos are known culinarily as rich, smoky chipotle peppers.'),
    ('JICAMA', 'Yam Bean Fruit', 'Starchy climbing vine that produces crisp, sweet, watery edible underground tubers.', 'Sliced raw and dusted with chili powder and lime juice as a Mexican street snack.'),
    ('JONAGOLD', 'Golden-Jonathan Cross', 'Large apple variety combining the sweet golden flavor of Golden Delicious with Jonathan tang.', 'Features a lovely red blush over yellow skin and honeyed tart flesh.'),
    ('JONAMAC', 'Sweet Autumn Apple', 'Cross between Jonathan and McIntosh bred in New York, ripening in early autumn.', 'Features dark red skin with sweet, aromatic flesh reminiscent of both parents.'),
    ('JONATHAN', 'Classic American Apple', 'Bright red heirloom apple with a lively, spicy, tart-sweet flavor balance.', 'Discovered in Woodstock, New York, in the 1820s; fantastic for fresh apple sauce.'),
    ('JUICE', 'Liquid Essence', 'The natural fluid, liquid, or moisture contained within fruit tissues.', 'Extracted by squeezing, pressing, or blending fresh ripe citrus and berries.'),
    ('JUJUBE', 'Chinese Date', 'Sweet oval fruit that turns wrinkled and chewy like a date when fully dried.', 'Cultivated in China for over 4,000 years; revered in traditional herbal medicine.'),
    ('KABOCHA', 'Japanese Pumpkin', 'Sweet Japanese winter squash with dark knobby green rind and dense orange flesh.', 'Sweeter than pumpkin with a fluffy, chestnut-like texture in tempura dishes.'),
    ('KABOSU', 'Japanese Green Citrus', 'Juicy Japanese citrus fruit used like lemon juice to season grilled fish.', 'Closely related to yuzu, harvested green to season sashimi and hot pot broths.'),
    ('KAFFIRLIME', 'Aromatic Citrus', 'Bumpy, wrinkled green citrus fruit whose aromatic double-leaves season Thai curries.', 'Leaves and zest provide an unmistakable citrus floral aroma to tom yum soups.'),
    ('KANDIS', 'Sour Garcinia', 'Small, bright yellow wild fruit used across Indonesia as a souring condiment.', 'Dried sliced rinds add fruity acidity to traditional Sumatran beef rendang.'),
    ('KASTURI', 'Borneo Black Mango', 'Small wild mango endemic to southern Borneo with purple-black skin.', 'Flesh is vibrant orange, fiberless, and celebrated for an intoxicating perfume aroma.'),
    ('KEITT', 'Giant Green Mango', 'Massive late-season mango that stays green with a slight pink blush when ripe.', 'Remains sweet and fiberless even when fruits grow to over two pounds in weight.'),
    ('KELEDANG', 'Bornean Orange Aril', 'Rare tropical fruit native to Borneo with rough skin and bright orange flesh.', 'Arils taste like a delicious sweet fusion of jackfruit, mango, and mangosteen.'),
    ('KENT', 'Sweet Late Mango', 'Large, sweet mango cultivar with dark green skin blushing red and fiberless pulp.', 'Originating in Florida; sweet, rich, and juicy with a long summer season.'),
    ('KEPEL', 'Perfume Fruit', 'Rare Indonesian fruit that was historically reserved for royal princesses.', 'Consuming the fruit was believed to give bodily sweat a pleasant violet aroma.'),
    ('KESAR', 'Saffron Mango', 'Renowned mango cultivar from Gujarat, India, celebrated for intense saffron aroma.', "Known as the 'Queen of Mangoes'; prized for making traditional Gujarati aamras."),
    ('KEYLIME', 'Small Floridian Lime', 'Small, spherical lime variety famous for intense aroma and tart yellow juice.', "The foundational ingredient of Florida's famous sweetened condensed milk Key Lime pie."),
    ('KINNOW', 'Pakistani Citrus', 'High-yield mandarin hybrid cultivated extensively in Punjab, Pakistan.', 'Known for extraordinarily juicy pulp and sweet flavor, exported across the Middle East.'),
    ('KISHU', 'Tiny Seedless Citrus', 'Miniature seedless mandarin variety smaller than a golf ball with sweet pulp.', 'One of the oldest citrus varieties in Japan, celebrated for kid-friendly snacking.'),
    ('KIWI', 'Chinese Gooseberry', 'Small oval fruit with fuzzy brown skin and vibrant emerald-green seeded flesh.', "Native to China; renamed kiwi in New Zealand after the country's national flightless bird."),
    ('KOKUM', 'Cooling Fruit', 'Dark purple fruit native to the Western Ghats of India used as a souring spice.', 'Dried rinds infuse curries and cool summer drinks like sol kadhi.'),
    ('KOSUI', 'Sweet Japanese Pear', 'The most popular russet Asian pear variety in Japan, sweet and very juicy.', 'Features a tender, fine-grained texture with rich natural sugar sweetness.'),
    ('KUMQUAT', 'Eat-Whole Citrus', 'Small olive-sized oval citrus fruit eaten entirely whole, including sweet peel.', 'The thin outer skin is deliciously sweet, while the inner juice vesicles are sour.'),
    ('KUNDANG', 'Plum Mango Fruit', 'Small oval fruit native to Southeast Asia with bright orange edible skin.', 'Young green fruits are pickled, while ripe orange fruits are sweet and eaten fresh.'),
    ('LANGRA', 'Vibrant Green Mango', 'Legendary Indian mango that remains lime-green even when completely sweet and ripe.', 'Originating in Varanasi; renowned for distinct citrus floral notes and silky texture.'),
    ('LANGSAT', 'Southern Asian Cluster', 'Small oval fruit with thin beige skin that peels away to reveal sweet segments.', 'Common street fruit across Thailand and Malaysia, sweet with gentle acidity.'),
    ('LAPINS', 'Jumbo Sweet Cherry', 'Large, dark mahogany-red sweet cherry with firm, split-resistant flesh.', 'Bred by crossing Van and Stella cherries; highly crack-resistant after summer rains.'),
    ('LEMON', 'Sour Citrus', 'Bright yellow citrus fruit prized worldwide for acidic juice and fragrant zest.', 'High citric acid content gives lemon juice its sharp sour taste in cooking and drinks.'),
    ('LEMONDROP', 'Mangosteen Relative', 'Bright yellow tropical fruit with sweet-tart pulp tasting like a lemon drop candy.', 'Bears heavy crops in tropical home gardens, eaten fresh by slicing peel in half.'),
    ('LIBERTY', 'Disease-Free Apple', 'Crisp, tart-sweet red apple cultivar bred for exceptional natural disease resistance.', 'Requires minimal pesticide spraying; beloved by organic homestead orchards.'),
    ('LIME', 'Green Citrus', 'Small, round green citrus fruit with sharp acidic juice and fragrant zest.', 'Essential ingredient in guacamole, key lime pies, ceviche marinades, and cocktails.'),
    ('LIMEQUAT', 'Citrus Dwarf Hybrid', 'Hybrid cross between a Key lime and a kumquat with sweet skin and sour juice.', 'Small oval fruit eaten entirely whole, combining sweet rind and acidic juice.'),
    ('LINGONBERRY', 'Boreal Berry', 'Small, tart red berry that grows on low evergreen shrubs across northern Scandinavia.', 'Traditionally served as a sweetened relish alongside Swedish meatballs and pancakes.'),
    ('LISBON', 'Thorny Lemon Tree', 'Cold-hardy lemon variety with smooth, thin skin and high acidic juice yields.', 'Dense tree foliage protects lemons from frost and high desert summer winds.'),
    ('LOGANBERRY', 'Heritage Hybrid', 'Accidental hybrid cross of blackberry and raspberry discovered in California in 1881.', 'Named after judge James Logan; produces elongated, deep red, pleasantly acidic berries.'),
    ('LONGAN', 'Dragon Eye', 'Small round fruit with a thin brown shell and translucent flesh around a dark seed.', "Called 'dragon eye' in Cantonese because the black seed shines through translucent flesh."),
    ('LOQUAT', 'Subtropical Pome', 'Small oval golden-orange fruit native to China with sweet, tangy juicy flesh.', 'Also known as Japanese plum; contains two to four smooth brown inner seeds.'),
    ('LUCUMA', 'Gold of the Incas', 'Subtropical Andean fruit with bright yellow dry flesh tasting like maple syrup.', 'The most popular ice cream flavor in Peru, dried into sweet nutrient-dense powder.'),
    ('LUFFA', 'Bath Sponge Gourd', 'Elongated gourd fruit that turns into a natural fibrous scrubbing sponge when dried.', 'Young immature gourds are eaten as a succulent vegetable in Chinese soups.'),
    ('LULO', 'Naranjilla', 'Subtropical fruit from the Andes with citrus-rhubarb jelly green pulp.', "The star ingredient in 'lulo juice', popular throughout Colombia and Ecuador."),
    ('LYCHEE', 'Sweet Soapberry', 'Small tropical fruit with a rough pinkish-red shell and translucent sweet white aril.', 'Native to southeastern China; celebrated for floral aroma and grape-like sweetness.'),
    ('MABOLO', 'Velvet Apple', 'Tropical fruit with velvety reddish-brown fur skin and sweet, dry cheese-like flesh.', 'Known as velvet persimmon; native to the Philippines with dark ebony wood.'),
    ('MAGNESS', 'Blight-Resistant Pear', 'High-quality dessert pear bred by USDA for exceptional fire blight resistance.', 'Rich, aromatic, melting sweet flesh with almost no grit cells in the pulp.'),
    ('MALBEC', 'Argentine Grape', 'Purple grape variety celebrated in Argentina for plush blackberry and cocoa flavors.', 'Thrives in high-altitude vineyards of Mendoza beneath the snowy Andes.'),
    ('MALIC', 'Apple Acid', 'Organic dicarboxylic acid contributing to the pleasantly sour taste of green apples.', "Derived from the Latin word 'malum' meaning apple; sharp and refreshing."),
    ('MALLIKA', 'Citrus Mango Hybrid', 'Indian mango hybrid combining Neelum and Dasheri with notes of citrus and melon.', 'Features fiberless, vibrant orange flesh with an exceptionally rich dessert flavor.'),
    ('MAMEY', 'Sapote Giant', 'Large oval fruit with sandpaper skin and creamy orange-coral flesh tasting of sweet potato.', 'A staple milkshake and dessert ingredient throughout Cuba and the Caribbean.'),
    ('MANDARIN', 'Small Citrus', 'Small, easy-to-peel sweet citrus fruit with distinct loose pebbled skin.', 'Traditional symbol of abundance and good fortune during Lunar New Year feasts.'),
    ('MANGO', 'King of Fruits', 'Juicy tropical stone fruit with sweet, golden flesh and an intoxicating fragrance.', 'The national fruit of India, Pakistan, and the Philippines; over 500 varieties exist.'),
    ('MANGOSTEEN', 'Queen of Fruits', 'Purple tropical fruit with a thick bitter rind enclosing juicy, snow-white segments.', "Known as the 'Queen of Fruits' for exquisite sweet-tangy peach-strawberry flavor."),
    ('MAPRANG', 'Sweet Mango Plum', 'Thai fruit resembling a miniature mango with sweet, juicy orange pulp.', 'Entire fruit including skin is eaten fresh, tasting like mango with a hint of plum.'),
    ('MAQUI', 'Patagonian Superberry', 'Small, deep purple-black berry native to the temperate rainforests of Chile.', 'Revered by the Mapuche people for centuries as a natural stamina enhancer.'),
    ('MARANG', 'Fragrant Wild Fruit', 'Tropical fruit native to Borneo and the Philippines covered in soft spines.', 'Once cracked open, emits a sweet scent and reveals snow-white melting arils.'),
    ('MARIONBERRY', 'Oregon Blackberry', 'Cultivar of blackberry bred in Marion County, Oregon, hailed as the king of blackberries.', 'Celebrated for complex, rich, earthy flavor profile in artisan berry pies.'),
    ('MARMALADE', 'Citrus Preserve', 'Fruit preserve made from the juice and peel of citrus fruits boiled with sugar.', 'Traditionally made with bitter Seville oranges to achieve iconic bittersweet balance.'),
    ('MAROLO', 'Savanna Custard Fruit', 'Large Brazilian savanna fruit with thick green rind and sweet yellow pulp.', 'Emits a powerful fruity aroma that perfumes entire rooms when fully ripe.'),
    ('MARRS', 'Early Texas Orange', 'Early-season sweet orange cultivar discovered as a limb sport in Texas in 1927.', 'Low in acid and seedless, producing heavy clusters of sweet juicy fruit.'),
    ('MARULA', 'African Tree Fruit', 'Golden-yellow African fruit with a tart flavor rich in Vitamin C.', 'A favorite feast for African elephants; fermented to make famous Amarula liqueur.'),
    ('MAYPOP', 'Wild Passionflower', 'Hardy purple passionflower fruit native to the southeastern United States.', "Named 'maypop' because the hollow fruits pop loudly when stepped on."),
    ('MCINTOSH', 'Ruby Red Apple', 'Classic red-and-green apple with tender, juicy white flesh and tart flavor.', "Discovered in Ontario in 1811; the namesake of Apple's Macintosh computer."),
    ('MEDLAR', 'Ancient Fruit', 'Brown pome fruit eaten in winter after undergoing a soft bletting decay process.', 'Popular across medieval Europe; develops a spiced apple butter flavor when bletted.'),
    ('MELOGOLD', 'Sweet Citrus Cross', 'Triploid citrus hybrid cross between a pomelo and grapefruit bred in California.', 'Sweeter and milder than standard grapefruit with thinner peel than pomelos.'),
    ('MELON', 'Gourd Fruit', 'Large sweet fleshy fruit growing on trailing vines with seeds in central cavity.', 'Encompasses watermelons, honeydews, cantaloupes, and sweet dessert melons.'),
    ('MELROSE', 'Ohio State Apple', 'The official State Apple of Ohio, bred by crossing Jonathan and Red Delicious.', 'Heavy winter apple that develops a rich, sweet, honey-like flavor in storage.'),
    ('MERLOT', 'Plum Wine Grape', 'Popular dark blue wine grape variety prized for soft, luscious plum flavors.', 'Its name derives from the French word for blackbird; pairs smoothly with food.'),
    ('MESOCARP', 'Middle Flesh', 'The middle fleshy layer of the pericarp of a fruit, between exocarp and endocarp.', 'Forms the thick, succulent, sweet edible part of peaches, mangoes, and plums.'),
    ('MESQUITE', 'Desert Bean Pod', 'Sweet, golden seed pod harvested from drought-hardy desert mesquite trees.', 'Ground into naturally sweet, gluten-free flour with caramel and molasses notes.'),
    ('METEOR', 'Cold-Hardy Tart Cherry', 'Spur-type sour cherry bred in Minnesota to survive harsh sub-zero prairie winters.', 'Produces large, bright red cherries with clear juice and small pits for pies.'),
    ('METHLEY', 'Sweet Early Plum', 'Early-ripening Japanese plum with reddish-purple skin and juicy sweet red flesh.', 'Heavy producer in early summer; delicious eaten fresh right off the branch.'),
    ('MEYER', 'Sweet Floral Lemon', 'Hybrid citrus cross of lemon and mandarin orange with thin skin and floral juice.', 'Much sweeter and less acidic than regular lemons; beloved by pastry chefs for curd.'),
    ('MINNEOLA', 'Honeybell Tangelo', 'Famous bell-shaped citrus hybrid of Darcy tangerine and Duncan grapefruit.', 'Prized for juicy sweetness and prominent raised neck; harvested in January.'),
    ('MIRABELLE', 'French Petite Plum', 'Small, sweet golden-yellow plum cultivated primarily in the Lorraine region of France.', 'Celebrated for making Mirabelle eau-de-vie fruit brandy, fruit tarts, and preserves.'),
    ('MONSTERA', 'Swiss Cheese Fruit', 'Elongated cone fruit from Monstera deliciosa tasting of banana and pineapple.', 'Must be eaten only when green scales naturally fall off to avoid oxalates.'),
    ('MONTMORENCY', 'Pie Tart Cherry', 'The gold standard sour pie cherry, featuring bright red skin and clear tart juice.', 'Grown extensively in Michigan and Wisconsin for cherry pies, jams, and juices.'),
    ('MOONGLOW', 'Early Blight Pear', 'Large yellow-bronze pear with soft, juicy white flesh and mild sweet aroma.', 'Excellent for home canning, salads, and fresh eating straight from the tree.'),
    ('MOORPARK', 'Heirloom Apricot', 'Historic English apricot variety celebrated for exceptional rich perfume flavor.', 'Cultivated since 1688 at Moor Park; renowned as one of the finest dessert apricots.'),
    ('MOREAU', 'French Sweet Cherry', 'Early-season dark sweet French cherry with firm, heart-shaped black fruit.', 'One of the earliest sweet cherries to hit farmers markets across southern France.'),
    ('MORICHE', 'Mauritia Palm Fruit', 'Scaly oval fruit harvested from the buriti palm tree across Amazonian swamps.', 'Packed with Vitamin A; eaten fresh or pressed into golden cosmetic buriti oil.'),
    ('MOURVEDRE', 'Bandol Red Grape', 'Thick-skinned red grape producing dark, earthy, gamey wines in Provence and Rhone.', 'Known as Mataro in Australia and California; thrives in scorching coastal sun.'),
    ('MULBERRY', 'Tree Berry', 'Sweet, elongated aggregate berry growing on deciduous Morus trees.', 'Silkworm caterpillars feed exclusively on the leaves of the white mulberry tree.'),
    ('MUNDU', 'Garcinia Fruit', 'Yellow-orange tropical fruit related to mangosteen native to Indonesia.', 'Features a pleasantly sweet and sour pulp used in jams and cooling drinks.'),
    ('MURCOTT', 'Honey Tangerine', 'Sweet late-season mandarin-orange hybrid known as the Honey Tangerine.', 'Rich in sugars and juice; the foundation of late winter Florida citrus sales.'),
    ('MUSCADINE', 'Southern Wild Grape', 'Large, thick-skinned grape native to the southeastern US with musky sweetness.', 'High in resveratrol; thrives in hot, humid Southern climates where other vines fail.'),
    ('MUSCAT', 'Ancient Perfume Grape', 'Ancient grape family renowned for its distinctive, sweet, unctuous floral grape scent.', 'One of the oldest domesticated grape varieties on Earth, dating back to antiquity.'),
    ('MUSKMELON', 'Aromatic Melon', 'Sweet, heavily scented melon species encompassing cantaloupes and honeydews.', 'Named for the rich, musky sweet fragrance emitted when fruits reach peak ripeness.'),
    ('MUTSU', 'Crisp Japanese Pome', 'Large, crisp greenish-yellow apple developed in Japan by crossing Golden and Indo.', 'Also known as Crispin; features sweet, honeyed flesh that keeps its shape in pies.'),
    ('MYRTLEBERRY', 'Mediterranean Drupe', 'Small, aromatic blue-black berry growing on fragrant wild myrtle shrubs.', 'Macerated in alcohol in Sardinia to produce traditional Mirto digestif liqueur.'),
    ('NAMDOKMAI', 'Thai Dessert Mango', 'Famous Thai mango cultivar with an elongated, sharply pointed teardrop shape.', 'The classic mango served across Thailand alongside warm sweet coconut sticky rice.'),
    ('NANCE', 'Yellow Golden Berry', 'Small, round yellow fruit with a pungent, sweet-tart aroma in Central America.', 'Fermented into festive chicha or eaten with shaved ice and sweetened milk.'),
    ('NASHI', 'Asian Sand Pear', 'Round, crisp Asian pear with golden-russet skin and high water content.', 'Eaten crisp like an apple rather than soft; exceptionally juicy and refreshing.'),
    ('NEBBIOLO', 'Piedmont King', 'Noble Italian grape variety behind the prestigious Barolo and Barbaresco wines.', "Named from 'nebbia' (fog) for the dense autumn mists shrouding Piedmont hills."),
    ('NECTAR', 'Sweet Liquid', 'Sugary fluid secreted by plants within flowers to encourage pollinator visits.', 'Bees collect floral nectar and transform it into rich golden honeycombs.'),
    ('NECTARINE', 'Smooth Peach', 'Genetic cultivar of the peach characterized by smooth, fuzz-free skin.', 'A recessive peach gene produces smooth skin without altering peach juicy sweetness.'),
    ('NEELUM', 'South Indian Mango', 'Late-season Indian mango cultivar renowned for smooth floral aroma and sweet pulp.', 'Bears heavy yields annually, highly prized for long shelf life during transit.'),
    ('NIJISSEIKI', 'Twentieth Century Pear', 'The most famous green-skinned Asian pear in Japan, crisp, juicy, and refreshing.', 'Round like an apple with delicate thin skin and sweet thirst-quenching juice.'),
    ('NONI', 'Cheese Fruit', 'Yellowish-white tropical fruit known for pungent, strong smell resembling rotten cheese.', 'Used in traditional Polynesian healing practices and bottled as wellness tonics.'),
    ('NOPAL', 'Cactus Pad and Fruit', 'The edible flat green pads and sweet fruits of the prickly pear cactus.', 'Used in traditional Mexican cooking as a tender savory vegetable and sweet fruit.'),
    ('NORTHERNSPY', 'Vintage Pie Apple', 'Famous 19th-century American pie apple with striped skin and tart, juicy flesh.', "Popular folk proverb says: 'Northern Spy, it's the only apple for pie!'"),
    ('NORTHSTAR', 'Dwarf Pie Cherry', 'Dwarf sour cherry tree bred at University of Minnesota for small home gardens.', 'Bears heavy crops of dark red cherries with red flesh and delicious tart flavor.'),
    ('NUTMEG', 'Aromatic Seed', 'Fragrant inner seed of a yellow tropical peach-like fruit on Myristica trees.', 'Grated freshly over custards, eggnog, pumpkin pies, and béchamel sauces.'),
    ('OKRA', 'Lady Finger Pod', 'Slender green ridged seed pod containing mucilaginous juice and edible round seeds.', 'Thickens traditional Southern gumbo stews; popular fried in crisp cornmeal.'),
    ('OLALLIE', 'California Blackberry', 'Blackberry hybrid bred in Oregon in 1935 and popularized in sunny California.', 'Produces sweet, glossy black berries prized for fresh crumbles and preserves.'),
    ('OLALLIEBERRY', 'California Bramble', 'Blackberry hybrid bred in 1935 producing sweet, glossy black fruit in California.', 'A staple of roadside fruit stands along Highway 1 in California during summer.'),
    ('OLIVE', 'Mediterranean Drupe', 'Small bitter fruit pressed to yield golden olive oil or cured in brine to eat.', 'Symbol of peace since antiquity; curing leaches out bitter compound oleuropein.'),
    ('OPAL', 'Golden Russet-Free', 'Vibrant yellow apple cultivar that naturally resists browning when sliced open.', 'Cross between Golden Delicious and Topaz with a floral, sweet-tart crunch.'),
    ('ORANGE', 'Citrus Fruit', 'Round citrus fruit famous for vibrant orange color and sweet, tangy juice.', 'Rich in immune-boosting Vitamin C; segmented pulp enclosed in an aromatic zest peel.'),
    ('ORCHARD', 'Fruit Grove', 'Intentional planting of trees or shrubs maintained for food fruit production.', 'Encompasses commercial apple, cherry, peach, pear, and citrus groves.'),
    ('ORLANDO', 'Early Tangelo', 'Mild, sweet citrus hybrid of tangerine and grapefruit with cupped leaves.', 'One of the earliest tangelos to mature in autumn, offering mild sweet juice.'),
    ('OROBIANCO', 'White Citrus Cross', 'Sweet white grapefruit-pomelo hybrid with thick rind and zero bitterness.', "Name means 'white gold' in Italian; segments can be eaten without adding sugar."),
    ('ORTANIQUE', 'Jamaican Tangor', 'Natural tangor hybrid discovered in Manchester, Jamaica, with rich sweet juice.', "Name combines 'Orange', 'Tangerine', and 'Unique'; possesses high sugar brix."),
    ('PACKHAM', 'Triumph Pear', 'Large, bumpy green pear variety with sweet, exceptionally juicy white flesh.', 'Bred in Australia in 1896; retains its green color even when fully ripe and sweet.'),
    ('PALMER', 'Late Season Red Mango', 'Large, elongated mango variety with red-purple skin and smooth sweet pulp.', 'Widely cultivated in Brazil for international export during northern winter months.'),
    ('PAPAYA', 'Tropical Melon', 'Large tropical fruit with sweet salmon-pink flesh and peppery black round seeds.', 'Contains papain, a natural proteolytic enzyme used as a meat tenderizer.'),
    ('PARSONBROWN', 'Historic Florida Orange', 'Historic early-season Florida sweet orange discovered in 1865 near Webster.', 'One of the foundational commercial varieties that built the Florida citrus trade.'),
    ('PASSIONFRUIT', 'Purple Tropics', 'Round purple tropical fruit filled with aromatic orange pulp and crunchy seeds.', 'Named by Spanish missionaries after the Passion of Christ due to floral symbolism.'),
    ('PAWPAW', 'American Custard Fruit', 'The largest edible fruit native to North America, growing wild in river valleys.', 'Features creamy golden-yellow custard flesh tasting like banana, mango, and melon.'),
    ('PEACH', 'Velvet Drupe', 'Juicy summer stone fruit with fuzzy velvety skin and sweet yellow or white flesh.', 'Originated in ancient China where it was revered as a sacred symbol of immortality.'),
    ('PEAR', 'Pome Fruit', 'Sweet, juicy bell-shaped fruit with soft, slightly granular melting flesh.', 'Ripens from the inside out; prized varieties include Bartlett, Bosc, and Anjou.'),
    ('PECAN', 'Southern Drupe', 'Sweet, rich buttery nut-like seed harvested from hickory trees in the US.', 'The iconic centerpiece of Southern pecan pies and praline confections.'),
    ('PECTIN', 'Natural Gelling', 'Soluble gelatinous polysaccharide found in ripe fruits used to set jams.', 'Apples, quinces, and citrus rinds are naturally high in jam-setting pectin.'),
    ('PEDALAI', 'Bornean Forest Fruit', 'Wild tropical rainforest tree fruit native to Borneo with orange-red flesh.', 'Arils are sweet and fragrant, while seeds can be roasted like chestnuts.'),
    ('PEEL', 'Outer Skin', 'The outer protective layer or skin of a fruit like an orange, banana, or apple.', 'Often rich in aromatic essential oils, bitter zest, and protective waxes.'),
    ('PEPE', 'Melon Pear', 'Also known as pepino melon, a sweet juicy South American fruit resembling melon.', 'Features cream-colored skin with purple stripes and cucumber-cantaloupe flavor.'),
    ('PEPI', 'Pepino Melon', 'Sweet, aromatic South American fruit with creamy yellow skin and purple streaks.', 'Has a crisp, refreshing flavor combining sweet cantaloupe and fresh cucumber.'),
    ('PEPPER', 'Capsicum Fruit', 'Fleshy hollow fruit ranging from sweet bell peppers to fiery habaneros.', 'Botanically berries; available in vibrant green, yellow, orange, and red colors.'),
    ('PERICARP', 'Fruit Wall', 'The entire wall of a fruit developed from the ovary wall enclosing the seeds.', 'Composed of three distinct layers: the outer exocarp, mesocarp, and inner endocarp.'),
    ('PERRY', 'Pear Cider', 'Alcoholic beverage made from fermented pear juice, similar to apple cider.', 'Crafted for centuries in England and France using traditional tart perry pears.'),
    ('PERSIMMON', 'Sweet Sharon Fruit', 'Glossy orange-red autumn fruit that turns honey-sweet when fully ripe.', 'Astringent Hachiya types must soften completely to jelly; Fuyu types can be eaten crisp.'),
    ('PHYSALIS', 'Cape Gooseberry', 'Bright orange berry enclosed within a delicate, papery lantern-like calyx.', 'Also called goldenberry; provides sweet-tart floral flavor to tarts and dipping chocolates.'),
    ('PINEAPPLE', 'Compound Tropical Fruit', 'Large tropical fruit with spiky crown, diamond rind, and sweet fibrous yellow pulp.', 'A multiple fruit formed from dozens of individual fused flowers on a central core.'),
    ('PINKERTON', 'Long-Necked Avocado', 'Elongated, pear-shaped avocado cultivar featuring heavy yields of creamy flesh.', 'Possesses a very small inner seed, yielding exceptional edible flesh per fruit.'),
    ('PINKLADY', 'Cripps Pink Apple', 'Trademarked crisp apple variety with a distinctive blushing pink skin and fizz tartness.', 'The first apple to be marketed under a brand name, requiring long sun exposure.'),
    ('PINOT', 'Burgundy Grape', 'Noble wine grape family encompassing Pinot Noir, Pinot Gris, and Pinot Blanc.', 'Pinot Noir is celebrated for delicate cherry, forest floor, and truffle aromas.'),
    ('PIPPIN', 'Newtown Apple', 'Historic American green-yellow apple grown by George Washington and Thomas Jefferson.', 'Exported to Queen Victoria; renowned for intense complex acidity and cider quality.'),
    ('PISTACHIO', 'Green Drupe Seed', 'Small green culinary nut enclosed within a partially split beige shell.', 'Native to Central Asia and the Middle East; prized for distinctive green tint.'),
    ('PITAHAYA', 'Central Cactus Fruit', 'Vibrant cactus fruit with white or magenta pulp and edible black seeds.', 'Harvested from climbing night-blooming cereus cacti in tropical climates.'),
    ('PITH', 'Spongy Layer', 'The white, spongy inner layer beneath the zest rind of citrus fruits.', 'Rich in dietary fiber and bioflavonoids; has a mild, slightly bitter taste.'),
    ('PITOMBA', 'Amazonian Fruit', 'Small, bright yellow fruit native to Brazil with juicy, sweet-tart pulp.', 'Popular in northeastern Brazil; eaten fresh or blended into chilled juices.'),
    ('PLANTAIN', 'Cooking Banana', 'Starchy, firm banana variety used as a staple vegetable in tropical cooking.', 'Cooked green as savory chips or fried when ripe and black as sweet maduros.'),
    ('PLUM', 'Smooth Drupe', 'Smooth-skinned stone fruit with sweet, juicy flesh ranging from purple to yellow.', 'Dried into sweet prunes; belongs to the Prunus genus along with cherries and peaches.'),
    ('PLUOT', 'Hybrid Stone Fruit', 'Complex fruit hybrid bred from cross-pollinating plums and apricots.', 'Inherits sweet plum juicy flesh with a delicate floral apricot fragrance.'),
    ('POBLANO', 'Ancho Pepper', 'Large, mild dark green chili pepper with rich, earthy, savory vegetable flavor.', 'The classic pepper stuffed for chiles rellenos; dried poblanos are called ancho chilies.'),
    ('POINTEDGOURD', 'Parwal Gourd', 'Small green gourd with pointed ends widely used in North Indian savory cooking.', 'Stuffed with spiced fillings or cooked with potatoes in traditional curries.'),
    ('POLLEN', 'Floral Dust', 'Fine powdery substance consisting of microscopic pollen grains produced by flowers.', 'Transferred by bees between blossoms to initiate fruit development and seed growth.'),
    ('POMACE', 'Fruit Residue', 'The solid remains of fruit after pressing for juice, cider, or winemaking.', 'Consists of skins, seeds, and pulp; often distilled into pomace brandies like grappa.'),
    ('POMEGRANATE', 'Jeweled Arils', 'Ancient round red fruit filled with hundreds of jewel-like ruby juice arils.', 'Revered across Greek mythology and ancient Persia as a symbol of fertility and life.'),
    ('POMELO', 'Giant Citrus', 'The largest of all citrus fruits, featuring a very thick rind and sweet, mild pulp.', 'Ancestor of the modern grapefruit, native to Southeast Asia and Malaysia.'),
    ('PONKAN', 'Chinese Honey Citrus', 'High-quality loose-skin mandarin variety widely grown throughout Asia.', 'Sweet, aromatic, and juicy with an open puffy rind that peels in one piece.'),
    ('PRESERVE', 'Jammed Fruit', 'Preparation of whole or chopped fruit cooked with sugar until thickened.', 'Preserves the summer fruit harvest for enjoyment throughout chilly winter months.'),
    ('PRESIDENT', 'Giant English Plum', 'Large, oval late-season European plum with deep purple skin and yellow flesh.', 'Introduced in Hertfordshire, England, in 1901; excellent for baking and jams.'),
    ('PRICKLYFRUIT', 'Cactus Pear', 'Spiny, sweet oval fruit growing on the flat pads of Opuntia prickly pear cacti.', 'Ruby-red sweet interior is strained to make refreshing cactus aguas frescas.'),
    ('PRIMA', 'Scab-Free Apple', 'Early-maturing disease-resistant apple with dark red blush over yellow skin.', 'Developed through cooperative university breeding for natural orchard health.'),
    ('PRIMITIVO', 'Puglian Red Grape', 'Deep, jammy red grape cultivated across Puglia in the heel of Italy.', 'Produces hearty, full-bodied wines with high alcohol and sweet plum notes.'),
    ('PROSECCO', 'Sparkling Glera', 'Sparkling Italian wine crafted from the Glera grape in the Veneto region.', 'Celebrated for fresh, floral bubbles with notes of green apple and white peach.'),
    ('PRUNE', 'Dried Plum', 'Sweet, chewy dried European plum variety known for promoting digestion.', 'Rich in potassium, soluble fiber, and sorbitol; enjoyed as a healthy snack.'),
    ('PUMPKIN', 'Autumn Squash', 'Round, ribbed orange winter squash celebrated in autumn pies and jack-o-lanterns.', 'Rich in Vitamin A; seeds can be roasted into crunchy, protein-rich pepitas.'),
    ('QUINCE', 'Aromatic Pome', 'Hard, knobby golden-yellow pome fruit with an intense floral perfume aroma.', 'Too astringent to eat raw; simmers into pink paste and fragrant quince jelly.'),
    ('RAINIER', 'Golden Yellow Cherry', 'Premium cherry cultivar with golden-yellow skin blushing bright pink and sweet honey flesh.', 'Bred in Washington State; possesses higher sugar brix than red sweet cherries.'),
    ('RAISIN', 'Dried Grape', 'Sweet dried grape produced by dehydrating table grapes in natural sunshine.', 'Concentrates natural grape sugars into chewy, energy-dense baking ingredients.'),
    ('RAMBAI', 'Cluster Fruit', 'Small, round tropical fruit hanging in long strings from tree trunks.', 'Features translucent sweet-sour flesh divided into three to five segments.'),
    ('RAMBUTAN', 'Hairy Tropical Fruit', 'Red tropical fruit covered in soft, pliable hair-like spines called spinterns.', "Name derives from the Malay word for 'hair'; reveals a sweet, translucent jelly aril."),
    ('RANGPUR', 'Mandarin Lime', 'Highly acidic citrus hybrid with orange peel and flesh used as a lime substitute.', 'Smells of mandarin and lime; used in Britain to flavor aromatic specialty gins.'),
    ('RASPBERRY', 'Hollow Core Berry', 'Delicate red or golden aggregate fruit that leaves its core receptacle behind when picked.', 'Features a hollow cup shape when harvested; sweet with a vibrant floral acidity.'),
    ('REDCURRANT', 'Translucent Red Berry', 'Translucent jewel-like red berries hanging in elegant cascading strings.', 'Their sharp tartness makes redcurrants a classic garnish for roasts and summer puddings.'),
    ('REDDELICIOUS', 'Striped Classic Apple', 'Historic American apple variety recognized by its conic shape and five base points.', 'Discovered in Iowa in 1872; iconic deep red skin and mild sweet flavor.'),
    ('REDGLOBE', 'Jumbo Table Grape', 'Large, round red table grape with firm, crisp flesh and large seeds.', 'A festive favorite across Asian markets during Lunar New Year celebrations.'),
    ('REDGOLD', 'Late Season Nectarine', 'Large freestone nectarine with golden yellow flesh and deep red skin blush.', 'One of the most widely planted commercial nectarines, noted for firm shipping quality.'),
    ('REDHAVEN', 'Early Summer Peach', 'Classic freestone peach with bright red skin over golden yellow flesh.', 'High-yielding orchard variety celebrated for sweet dessert flavor and firm texture.'),
    ('REED', 'Giant Round Avocado', 'Large, spherical summer avocado variety with thick, pebbly green skin.', 'Can grow as large as a softball; remains green when ripe with exceptional butter flavor.'),
    ('RIDGEGOURD', 'Angled Luffa', 'Dark green ridged vegetable gourd widely cultivated across Southern Asia.', 'Known as tori or luffa acutangula; peeled and simmered in spiced savory stews.'),
    ('RIESLING', 'Floral White Grape', 'Aromatic white grape variety originating in Germany with piercing floral perfume.', 'Capable of aging for decades; reflects vineyard terroir with notes of slate and lime.'),
    ('RIND', 'Tough Peel', 'The thick, tough outer protective covering of melons, citrus, and cheeses.', 'Shields delicate inner juicy pulp from drying out in scorching summer heat.'),
    ('ROMA', 'Plum Tomato', 'Elongated, egg-shaped plum tomato with thick flesh and few interior seeds.', 'The classic culinary choice for cooking thick tomato sauces and canning paste.'),
    ('ROME', 'Baker Apple', 'Round, glossy red heirloom apple historically hailed as the finest baking apple.', 'Holds its shape firmly when baked whole with cinnamon and brown sugar.'),
    ('ROSEAPPLE', 'Water Apple', 'Bell-shaped tropical fruit with crisp, watery flesh and a delicate rosewater scent.', 'Popular thirst-quencher across Southeast Asia; eaten raw with spiced salt.'),
    ('ROWAN', 'Mountain Berry', 'Scarlet-red pome berry growing in dense clusters on European mountain ash trees.', 'High in Vitamin C; traditionally cooked into bitter-tart jellies for wild game.'),
    ('ROYALANN', 'Napoleon Cherry', 'Large, sweet cherry with golden-yellow skin blushing crimson and firm flesh.', 'The historic cultivar preferred for crafting gourmet maraschino cocktail cherries.'),
    ('RUSSET', 'Rough Skinned Apple', 'Historic apple variety characterized by rough, sandpaper-like bronze skin.', 'Possesses a rich, nutty, aromatic flavor prized for artisanal hard ciders.'),
    ('SALAK', 'Snakefruit', 'Teardrop fruit covered in overlapping reddish-brown scaly skin like a snake.', 'Snapping off the tip reveals three crisp garlic-shaped cloves with an apple-pineapple crunch.'),
    ('SALMONBERRY', 'Pacific Bramble', 'Moisture-loving bramble berry native to Pacific Northwest forests.', 'Produces golden-yellow to ruby-red berries shaped like raspberries, eaten by coastal bears.'),
    ('SALUSTIANA', 'Sweet Spanish Orange', 'Early-ripening seedless sweet orange discovered in Enova, Spain, in 1950.', 'Produces high yields of sweet, clear juice ideal for fresh morning squeezing.'),
    ('SANGIOVESE', 'Chianti Grape', "Italy's most planted red grape, the signature variety in Chianti Classico and Brunello.", 'Produces savory wines with high acidity, firm tannins, and notes of sour red cherry.'),
    ('SANMARZANO', 'Italian Plum Tomato', 'Famous Italian heirloom plum tomato grown in volcanic soils near Mount Vesuvius.', 'Prized by master pizza chefs for balanced sweetness, low acidity, and rich sauce set.'),
    ('SANTOL', 'Cotton Fruit', 'Tropical fruit with a thick rind and pillowy, cotton-like sweet-sour pulp.', 'The translucent white pulp around the seeds is sucked for refreshing flavor.'),
    ('SAPODILLA', 'Chiku', 'Brown tropical fruit with grainy, sweet pulp tasting like brown sugar and pear.', 'The latex sap of the sapodilla tree was historically tapped to make natural chicle chewing gum.'),
    ('SASKATOON', 'Prairie Berry', 'Native Canadian prairie pome fruit related to apples with deep purple skin.', 'Celebrated across Western Canada in traditional sweet saskatoon berry pies.'),
    ('SATSUMA', 'Juicy Mandarin', 'Cold-hardy, seedless mandarin variety with tender, exceptionally juicy pulp.', 'Originating from Satsuma province in Japan; ripens very early in autumn.'),
    ('SATURN', 'Donut Peach', 'Saucer-shaped flat peach variety with sunken center and creamy white sweet flesh.', 'Also known as the bagel peach or UFO peach; easy to eat without peeling.'),
    ('SAUVIGNON', 'Aromatic Grape', 'Green grape variety renowned for vibrant herbal aromas and crisp citrus acidity.', 'Sauvignon Blanc is famous in New Zealand for gooseberry and passionfruit notes.'),
    ('SEABUCKTHORN', 'Thorny Orange Berry', 'Vibrant orange berry packed with oils and Vitamin C growing on spiny coastal shrubs.', 'Juiced for tangy golden wellness tonics and used in high-end cosmetic skincare creams.'),
    ('SECKEL', 'Sugar Pear', 'Tiny, chubby heirloom pear renowned as the sweetest of all pear varieties.', 'Can be eaten whole in two bites, core and all; delicious pickled in spiced syrup.'),
    ('SEED', 'Reproductive Unit', 'Embryonic plant enclosed in a protective outer coat inside a fruit.', 'Can be tiny and edible like in kiwis or large and stone-like like in peaches.'),
    ('SEMILLON', 'Golden French Grape', 'Golden-skinned grape variety used in Bordeaux white blends and sweet Sauternes.', "Susceptible to beneficial 'noble rot' fungus that concentrates sweet honeyed flavors."),
    ('SERRANO', 'Mountain Chili Pepper', 'Crisp, bright green chili pepper sharper and hotter than the classic jalapeno.', 'Finely diced raw into fresh pico de gallo salsas and guacamole in Mexico.'),
    ('SERVICE', 'Juneberry', 'Sweet purple-blue pome fruit closely resembling a blueberry in size and hue.', 'Grows wild on Amelanchier trees; tastes of sweet blueberry and mild almond.'),
    ('SERVICEBERRY', 'Juneberry Pome', 'Sweet purple pome fruit resembling blueberries hanging on small woodland trees.', 'Tastes like sweet blueberry accented by a mild nutty hint of almond.'),
    ('SEVILLE', 'Bitter Marmalade Orange', 'Bitter, sour orange variety prized for making traditional English orange marmalade.', 'High natural pectin content and bitter essential oils produce perfect marmalade set.'),
    ('SHAMOUTI', 'Palestine Orange', 'Oval, nearly seedless sweet orange with thick leathery peel and fragrant juice.', 'The premier export orange of the Levant region throughout the 20th century.'),
    ('SHINSEIKI', 'New Century Pear', 'Bright yellow Asian pear cultivar with crisp, sweet, and mild white flesh.', "Ripens early in summer; name translates to 'New Century' in Japanese."),
    ('SHIRAZ', 'Australian Grape', 'The Australian name for the Syrah grape, producing bold, peppery red wines.', 'Old-vine Barossa Valley Shiraz wines are among the most celebrated globally.'),
    ('SHIRO', 'Golden Yellow Plum', 'Round, sweet yellow Japanese plum with translucent skin and very juicy flesh.', 'Introduced by legendary plant breeder Luther Burbank in California in 1899.'),
    ('SILVERBERRY', 'Wolf Willow Fruit', 'Dry, mealy silver-scaled berry fruit growing on native prairie riverbank shrubs.', 'A valuable winter wildlife forage for songbirds and small forest mammals.'),
    ('SKEENA', 'Firm Dark Cherry', 'Late-season dark sweet cherry with kidney shape and exceptionally firm bite.', 'Bred in Summerland, British Columbia, for long shelf life and sweet flavor.'),
    ('SLOE', 'Wild Blackthorn Berry', 'Small, astringent blue-black wild plum growing on spiny blackthorn bushes.', 'Steeped in gin with sugar to produce traditional English crimson sloe gin.'),
    ('SNAKEGOURD', 'Serpentine Fruit', 'Long, twisted green gourd fruit that resembles a dangling snake on vine trellises.', 'Popular in Indian and Southeast Asian cuisine, cooked in curries and lentil dahls.'),
    ('SNOOT', 'Stone Fruit', 'A common regional name for wild drupe fruits found in hedgerows.', 'Yields rustic jams and compotes in traditional rural European homesteads.'),
    ('SOURCHERRY', 'Baking Drupe', 'Acidic species of Prunus cerasus cultivated for pies, jams, and brandies.', 'Lower in sugar and higher in acid than sweet cherries, retaining vibrant red color.'),
    ('SOURORANGE', 'Seville Bitter', 'Rough-skinned sour orange widely grown for aromatic peel, blossoms, and marmalade.', 'Essential for Cuban mojo marinades, orange flower water, and curacao liqueurs.'),
    ('SOURSOP', 'Guanabana', 'Large spiny green fruit with fibrous, creamy white pulp tasting of citrus and berry.', 'Popular across the Caribbean for refreshing soursop smoothies and ice creams.'),
    ('SPARTAN', 'Sweet McIntosh Child', 'Small, sweet, dark purple-red apple developed in British Columbia in 1936.', 'A cross between McIntosh and Newtown Pippin with crisp, fragrant white flesh.'),
    ('SPONGEGOURD', 'Luffa Vine', 'Long green vine gourd whose fibrous interior vascular system forms bath luffas.', 'Harvested young and tender as a sweet culinary squash in Asian stir-fries.'),
    ('SQUASH', 'Vine Fruit', 'Fleshy gourd fruit cultivated in summer and winter varieties on creeping vines.', 'Encompasses butternut, acorn, kabocha, pumpkin, and tender green zucchini.'),
    ('STANLEY', 'Prune Plum', 'European plum cultivar with deep purple skin and dense, sweet yellow-green flesh.', 'Freestone plum excellent for fresh eating, baking tarts, and drying into prunes.'),
    ('STARAPPLE', 'Caimito', 'Round purple or green tropical fruit revealing a star pattern when sliced across.', 'Milky, sweet translucent pulp eaten chilled with a spoon in tropical gardens.'),
    ('STARFRUIT', 'Carambola', 'Oblong tropical fruit with five prominent ridges that forms stars when sliced crosswise.', 'Crisp, juicy flesh with a sweet-tart flavor; entire fruit including waxy skin is edible.'),
    ('STELLA', 'Self-Fertile Sweet Cherry', 'The first self-fertile sweet dark cherry variety bred in British Columbia.', 'Allows gardeners to harvest sweet black cherries from a single backyard tree.'),
    ('STEM', 'Fruit Stalk', 'The slender plant stalk connecting a hanging fruit to its parent branch.', 'Transports water and sweet carbohydrates as fruit grows and matures on the vine.'),
    ('STRAND', 'Berry String', 'Slender cascading string of individual berries hanging together on a stem.', 'Encountered when picking strings of glistening redcurrants and blackcurrants.'),
    ('STRAWBERRY', 'Aggregate Berry', 'Sweet, heart-shaped red fruit with tiny seed-like achenes on outer skin.', 'Botanically an aggregate accessory fruit whose seeds sit directly on red flesh.'),
    ('SUDACHI', 'Tokushima Citrus', 'Small, round green citrus fruit native to Tokushima Prefecture in Japan.', 'Prizewinning Japanese sour citrus whose fragrant juice elevates udon and soba.'),
    ('SULTANA', 'Golden Raisin', 'Pale amber dried seedless grape noted for juicy softness and sweet flavor.', 'Treated with vegetable oil and warm air to preserve its golden translucent hue.'),
    ('SUNBURST', 'Sweet Florida Tangerine', 'Dark orange, easy-to-peel tangerine hybrid bred by crossing two citrus crosses.', 'Bears heavy crops in November and December; sweet with high juice volume.'),
    ('SUNCREST', 'Flavorful Heirloom Peach', "Celebrated heirloom yellow peach made famous in the book 'Epitaph for a Peach.'", 'Possesses an authentic, old-fashioned balance of sweet peach sugars and acidity.'),
    ('SWEETANGO', 'Crisp Minnesotan', 'Modern apple cultivar bred from Honeycrisp and Zestar with explosive juicy snap.', 'Features vibrant red coloring and notes of brown sugar, honey, and spice.'),
    ('SWEETCHERRY', 'Fresh Orchard Drupe', 'Species of Prunus avium cultivated for delicious fresh hand snacking.', 'Grown in temperate valleys globally; includes Bing, Rainier, and Stella types.'),
    ('SWEETIE', 'Israeli Green Citrus', 'Sweet green citrus fruit bred in Israel by crossing grapefruit with pomelo.', 'Also called Oroblanco; stays bright green even when fully sweet and ripe.'),
    ('SWEETSOP', 'Sugar Apple', 'Sweet tropical fruit with knobby greenish-grey segmented rind and creamy pulp.', 'Breaks apart easily when ripe, revealing sweet, fragrant sugar-custard segments.'),
    ('SYCONIUM', 'Fig Structure', 'Fleshy hollow stem structure bearing multiple flowers internally like a fig.', 'The unique inverted floral structure characteristic of the Ficus plant family.'),
    ('SYRAH', 'Dark Spiced Grape', 'Dark-skinned red grape variety celebrated for blackberry, pepper, and smoke notes.', 'Known as Shiraz in Australia; produces full-bodied wines with firm tannins.'),
    ('TABASCO', 'Louisiana Chili', 'Small, intensely juicy chili pepper famous for flavoring iconic Tabasco pepper sauce.', 'Aged for three years in white oak whiskey barrels with salt on Avery Island.'),
    ('TAHITILIME', 'Persian Lime', 'The primary seedless commercial lime sold in Western grocery supermarkets.', 'Triploid hybrid cross; larger than Key lime with smooth, dark green skin.'),
